CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1775577779
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     GG4/12
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Soviet troops could begin their
OL,6, withdrawal from Afghanistan on May 15.
OL,8,FThe announcement was made in a joint
OL,9,Fstatement from the Soviet leader, Mr
OL,10,FMikhail Gorbachev, and the Afghan
OL,11,FPresident, Mr Najibullah, after they
OL,12,Fmet in the Soviet city of Tashkent.
OL,14,FThey said the withdrawal would go
OL,15,Fahead provided a UN peace accord
OL,16,Fcould be signed as soon as possible.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThere were no longer any obstacles to
OL,19,Fthe signing of accords between Pakistan
OL,20,Fand Afghanistan and at UN-sponsored
OL,21,Fpeace talks in Geneva, they added.
OL,23,T]Cfrom 07-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18105
SC,0005
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1775577779
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/12
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, Recent differences between the Soviet
OL,6, Union and the United States had cast
OL,7, doubts on a Soviet-Afghan agreement.
OL,9,FThe US said it would continue to give
OL,10,Faid to Moslem rebels fighting in Kabul
OL,11,Fif Moscow did not stop sending arms to
OL,12,Fthe Afghan government, but the Kremlin
OL,13,Fsaid this would be unacceptable.
OL,15,FToday's statement suggested the
OL,16,Fdifferences had been resolved.
OL,18,FPakistani President Zia ul-Haq said the
OL,19,FUSSR and the US had solved the problem
OL,20,Fby agreeing to continue to supply arms
OL,21,Fto their respective allies.
OL,23,T]Cfrom 07-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
